AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC> "The process of separating components by high-performance liquid chromatography."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_analytical_scale_fraction_collector> "An HPLC fraction collector that directs the eluant from an analytical scale HPLC experiment.

[James & Satya: 01/31/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_autosampler> "An HPLC component that is programmed to automatically inject samples into the HPLC column. 

[James & Satya: 01/31/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_buffer> "A parameter that identifies the elution buffer used in HPLC. A mixture of buffers is often prepared in a mixing device to form a time-dependent elution gradient.  

The HPLC_buffer parameter is a substance identifier, which points to an instance of 'solution'.  A 'solution' is_described_by one or more mixture_component_descriptor(s), each of which has two parts:  the component_amount and a substance_identifier that specifies the identity of the component.  This is a flexible way of describing solutions.  For example, a solution can be described as a mixture of two other solutions (e.g., buffer A and buffer B), in which case the mixture_component_descriptor(s) each specify the identity and amount of each of these buffers.  Alternatively, a solution can be described according to the concentrations of its solutes (molecules), each of which is specified by a mixture_component_descriptor.   In this case, complete description of the solution requires that the solvent be specified using the property has_solvent, which points to an instance of the class 'solvent'.

[James & Satya: 01/31/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_chromatogram> "A data collection (chromatogram) generated by an HPLC experiment -This typically consists of a collection of time/signal intensity pairs 

[James & Satya: 03/29/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_chromatogram_XML_format_data> "A data collection (chromatogram) generated by an HPLC experiment - This describes, two-column data which are signal vs time. The data columns are in XML.

[James & Satya: 03/29/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_chromatogram_text_format_data> "A data collection (chromatogram) generated by an HPLC experiment - This describes, two-column data which are signal vs time. The data columns are generally tab, space or comma separated.

[James & Satya: 03/29/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_column> "A matrix-containing tube  that is used for high-performance liquid chromatography.  The sample is separated into its components by injecting it into the column and elutimng with a solvent or buffer."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_component> "A component of a hgh-performance liquid chromatograph"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_data_collection> "A data collection used or generated by a high performance liquid chromatography experiment"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_data_processing_application> "Application software used in processing/manipulating HPLC data.

[James & Satya: 03/27/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_detection_wavelength> "A parameter that describes the detection wavelength of the HPLC detector, which may be either an absorbance detector or a fluorescence detector.

[James & Satya: 01/31/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_detector> "An HPLC instrument component that detects molecules that are eluted from the HPLC column.

[James & Satya: 01/31/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_detector_signal> "A parameter that describes the detector signal measured at a particular time of an HPLC experiment."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_diode_array_detector> "A type of HPLC detector.

[James & Satya: 01/31/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#HPLC_excitation_wavelength> "A parameter that describes the excitation  wavelength of a fluorescence HPLC detector.

[James & Satya: 01/31/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
