[James & Satya: 03/27/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#Turbo_Sequest_application> "Application software developed by ThermoElectron for processing mass spectrometer data.

[James & Satya: 03/27/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#UNIPROT_accession_number> "A parameter that specifies the unique identifier for a particular protein in the UNIPROT (formerly SWISSPROT) database.
URL: www.uniprot.org/

[Dr. York & Satya: 06/14/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#URL_parameter> "A string parameter that specifies the location of a resource (such as a data file) on the internet - I.e., a Universal Resource Locator"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#UV_spectrometer> "An instrument that measures the transmittance of ultraviolet light through a sample (usually a liquid)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#absolute_amount> "A parameter describing the amount of a substance in absolute terms (total mass, total volume, total number of moles, as appropriate).

[will & satya 04/13/06]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#absolute_mass> "A parameter describing the total mass of a particular substance (e.g., 5 grams of NaCl) in a molecular aggregate"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#absolute_volume> "A parameter describing the total volume of a particular substance (e.g., 5 Liters of water) in a molecular aggregate"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#agent> "An agent is a real world object that causes something to happen, i.e., it initiates or implements a process.  Examples are human operators, analytical instruments, enzymes, and software applications"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#amino_acid_sequence> "A parameter describing the sequence of amino acid residues of a peptide or protein.  Amino acids are listed starting at the N-terminus and continuing to the C-terminus using standard one-letter amino acid nomenclature. The name of the amino acid sequence is same as the sequence string.

[Dr. York & Satya: 06/10/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#analytical_data_simulation> "The simulation of the output of an analytical instrument like NMR, ms or chromatography. It is computed based on a set of input parametres.

[Dr. York & Satya: 11/21/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#analytical_instrument> "An analytical instrument is a piece of hardware designed to measure a parameter or analyze a sample."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#annotation_parameter> "A parameter used in the annotation of data"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#antibody_affinity_HPLC_column> "A type of HPLC column"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#archaea> "Organisms, including the Crenarchaeota, Euryarchaeota and Korarchaeota, with a cell structure that is similar to other prokaryotes, but with some biochemical features  that are similar to eukaryotes, some similar to bacteria, and some unique to archaea."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#bacteria> "A diverse group of prokaryotic organisms, distinct from the Archaea."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#binary_HPLC_pump> "A type of HPLC pump.

[James & Satya: 01/31/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#biochemical_component_separation> "The task of physcially spearating the components of a mixture."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#biochemical_sample> "A molecular aggregate that has been prepared in the laboratory from a biological continuant."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#biological_continuant> "This class includes organisms at various stages of development or life-cycle (e.g., spore, seed, blastula, embryo, adult, epimastigote) and parts of these organisms (e.g., organs, tissues and cells).  It also includes cultured cells and tissues (e.g., cultured embryonic stem cells).
The ProPreO is not meant to explicitly describe all of these objects.  Rather, it is meant to provide access to ontological descriptions of these objects by defining broad classes that are more fully modeled in other ontologies."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#biological_source_parameter> "A parameter that describes some aspect of part of an organism that was used as the source of a biological_sample or biomolecule.  A biological source parameter refers to, for example, a species, organ, cell type, life-cycle stage, develomental stage, etc.  Within the context of ProPreO, biological source parameters are meant to describe  laboratory samples that are analyzed by or used in proteomics or glycoproteomics methods."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#calculated_parameter> "This describes the parameters created by an algorithm. For example, the score of a database search application namely MASCOT.

[Will & satya 10/16/06]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#capillary_HPLC_pump> "A type of HPLC pump.

[James & Satya: 01/31/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#cell> "A cell, such as a neutrophil or a stem cell.  These are more fully modeled in the cell ontology
http://obo.sourceforge.net/cgi-bin/detail.cgi?cell"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#chemical_abstracts_accession_number> "A parameter that corresponds to the Chemical Abstrracts Accession number of a molecule."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#chemical_agent> "A chemical agent is a chemical or molecule (such as an enzyme) that implements or initiates a molecular process."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#chemical_entity> "A material continuant that is described chiefly with respect to its chemical composition."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#chromatography> "The process of separating components by chromatography.

[Dr. York & Satya: 11/21/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#component_amount> "A parameter describing the amount of a substance in a mixture.  This is expressed as some sort of fractional amount, such as weight percent, molarity, etc."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#components_identification> "The complex task of identifhying the components of a mixture. This may involve, for example, HPLC of the mixture (i.e. separate_by_HPLC) followed by computational peak picking and peak matching (i.e., classify_data)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#components_quantification> "The complex task of quantifying the components of a mixture. This may involve, for example,
HPLC of the mixture (i.e. separate_by_HPLC) followed by computational peak picking and signal integration (i.e., quantify_data)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#computational_task> "A task involved in the processing of data by a computational application.

[Dr. York & Satya: 11/21/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#concentration_units> "A parameter defining the physical units of concentration"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#contour_plot> "A graphical plot in which the z-value is plotted as a function of the x- and y-values."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#creation_timestamp> "R"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#cyclotron_analyzer> "A type of MS analyzer"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#data> "Data constitute the basic units of information. Data can include collections of information or individual units of information.  Data can be experimental (measured) or theoretical (calculated).

[satya 02/15/06]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#data_classification> "The computational processing in which data elements are matched to a specific group to which they belong.  This  includes:
a) identifying molecules associated with experimental data features such as ion masses (e.g., MASCOT analysis)
b) categorize features in data using a set of parameters. For example, distinguish peptides from glycopeptides

[Dr. York & Satya: 11/21/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#data_collection> "This defines a broad class that includes any collection of data. It can hold other data collections, it can hold parameters, which are defined as atomic objects in ProPreO (i.e., parameters cannot be further subdivided.)

[Will & Satya 02/15/06]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#data_file_URL> "A string parameter that contains the URL of a data file."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#data_filtering> "This process selects parts of given data based on set of constraints.

[Will & Satya 10/24/06]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#data_format_transformation> "The task of transforming the format of data, usually creating a new data file with either new file format or data encoding.

[Dr. York & Satya: 11/21/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#data_processing> "The task of processing data using computational applications.

[Dr. York & Satya: 11/21/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#data_processing_application> "Application software used in processing/manipulating data.

