AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#mass_percent> "A parameter describing the amount of a particular substance in a mixture. 
    The mass percent of the substance is its percent contribution to the  
    total mass of the mixture.  Sometimes mass percent is called weight/weight 
    percent, and abbreviated %w/w."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#mass_spectrometer> "A mass spectrometer separates and counts ions based on their mass to charge ratios.

[James & Satya: 03/27/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#mass_to_charge_ratio> "A parameter describing the (measured or theoretical) mass-to-charge ratio (m/z) of a particular ion."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#mass_units> "A parameter defining the physical units of mass"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#mass_volume_percent> "A parameter describing the amount of a particular substance in a solution. 
    The mass-volume percent of the substance is usually expressed as the number of grams of the substance divided by the number of milliliters of the solution, all divided by 100.  Sometimes the mass-volume percent is abbreviated %w/v."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#material_continuant> "A material continuant is a real-world object."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#meta_data_file_URL> "A string parameter that contains the URL of a meta-data file."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#micromass_pkl_ms-ms_peak_list> "A data collection consisting of a list of precursor ion masses and associated fragment ion masses from an ms/ms experiment.

QTof users can export peak list data in either DTA or PKL format using the Micromass ProteinLynx package. 

The PKL format is similar to the DTA file format, but supports multiple MS/MS datasets in a single file. The first line of a PKL dataset contains the observed m/z, intensity, and charge state of the precursor peptide as a triplet of space separated values. Subsequent lines contain space separated pairs of fragment ion m/z and intensity values. 

Multiple MS/MS datasets are delimited by at least one blank line. 
(Reference: http://www.matrixscience.com/help/data_file_help.html#QTOF)

[James & Satya: 03/27/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#mixture> "A molecular aggregate composed of more than one type of molecule.

 A mixture is_described_by one or more mixture_component_descriptor(s), each of
which has two parts:  the component_amount and a substance_identifier that specifies the component itself."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#mixture_component_descriptor> "A pair of parameters that describes the amount of a particular component of a mixture.  For example '0.5 M NaCl' describes the amount of sodium chloride in a solution - there are two parts to this description - 0.5 M specifies the amount (half molar) - NaCl identifies the component that is present at that concentration."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#molarity> "A parameter describing the amount of a substance in a solution.  The molarity is the number of moles of the substance that is dissolved in one Liter of the solution."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#mole_fraction> "A parameter describing the amount of a substance in a solution.  The mole fraction is the number of moles of a particular solute divided by the total number of moles of in the solution."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#molecular_aggregate> "An aggregate of molecules, which may or may not be homogeneous.  E.G.:
 a liter of water (homogeneous)
 a pound of wheat flour (heterogeneous)
 a milligram of extracted protein (heterogeneous)

[will & satya 03/02/06]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#molecular_data_simulation> "The computational simulation of the structure, physical properties or behavior of a molecule, such as conformational trajectory or reaction kinetics.

[Dr. York & Satya: 11/21/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#molecular_description> "Describes the molecule, its properties, origin etc.

[Dr. York & Satya: 06/13/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#molecular_parameter> "A parameter describing the identity or a physical property of a molecule.

[James & Satya: 04/01/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#molecular_sequence> "A parameter describing the sequence of residues in a biopolymer.

[Dr. York & Satya: 06/28/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#molecule> "An  individual molecule, categorized according to a few broadly defined classes.

[Dr. York & Satya: 06/10/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#ms-ms_peak_list> "A data collection consisting of a list of precursor ion masses and associated fragment ion masses from an ms/ms experiment. Often, the abundance of the ion is included in the peak list.  The ms/ms peak list can be used to perform database searching or denovo sequencing.

[James & Satya: 03/27/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#ms_data_recording> "Tthe physical task of running a mass spectrometer on a specific sample and recording the resulting spectra.

[Dr. York & Satya: 11/21/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#ms_data_simulation> "Tthe simulation of mass spectra. For example, calculation of an isotopic distribution based on elemental composition and subsequent simulation of a mass spectum based on the calculated isotopic distribution.

[Dr. York & Satya: 11/21/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#ms_output_data_collection> "A data collection generated by a mass spectrometer or mass spectral data processing application"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#ms_processed_data> "A collection of mass spectral data that has been computationally processed - E.G. a peak list

[James & Satya: 03/22/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#ms_raw_data> "A collection of mass spectral data that has NOT been computationally processed other than to change its digital format"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#mzXML_ms_raw_data> "A collection of mass spectral data that has NOT been computationally processed, except that it has been converted to mzXML format"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#nanoflow_HPLC_pump> "A type of HPLC pump.

[James & Satya: 01/31/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#normal-phase_HPLC_column> "A type of HPLC column"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#oligopeptide> "A biomolecule composed of amino acids connected by amide bonds.  A peptide can be generated by fragmentation of a protein by a protease (e.g. trypsin).  In ProPreO, peptides are distinguished from proteins mainly by size (oligopeptides are smaller, and thereby distinct from polypeptides).

[Dr. York & Satya: 06/10/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#operating_parameter> "A parameter that is used to control the execution of a task, such as a physical parameter required for recording a mass spectrum or a computational parameter for processing a data set."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#operating_parameter_collection> "A data collection that is used to control the execution of a task, such as the physical parameters required for recording a mass spectrum or the computational parameters for processing a data set."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#organ> "A specific biological organ, such as heart or leaf.

Several OBO ontologies model anatomical features of organsims, including their organs, tissues, cells, etc.  and additional semantic information can be specified by cross reference to these other ontologies."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#organic_solvent_molecule> "A solvent molecule that contains carbon, e.g., methanol."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#organism> "A biological species, such as Homo sapiens or Arabidopsis thaliana.
The taxonomic classification of a biological species are modeled in other ontologies. 
http://obo.sourceforge.net/cgi-bin/detail.cgi?ncbi_taxonomy
http://obo.sourceforge.net/cgi-bin/detail.cgi?newt

Instances of specific organisms may be specified iwithin ProPreO, but their complete systematic taxonomy should be found in these other ontologies.

[Dr. York & Satya: 06/28/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#parameter> "In ProPreO, a parameter is a single, indivisible datum (i.e., parameters cannot be further subdivided.) Collections of parameters are called data_collections in ProPreO.

Note that in ProPreO, a parameter (such as a substance_identifier or biological_source_parameter) may refer to a specific object (such as an organism or a molecule), but the parameter and the object that it refers to are separate.  In these cases, the parameter is piece of information that may be found, for example, in a data file and the object it points to is a real world object of class of objects.  These two entities are related by the property 'refers_to_material_continuant'.

[satya 02/15/06]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#parent_ion> "An ion, generated in a mass spectrometer, that is subsequently dissociated into fragment ions in an MS/MS experiment"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#peptide_sequence_format_transformation> "This describes the tranformation of a given peptide sequence from one format into another.

[Dr. York & Satya: 11/21/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#person> "A human who initiates or implementes a task."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#physical_task> "A task that is performed by a human or physical instrument working on a 
physical sample."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#physical_units> "A parameter defining the physical units of a parameter (measurement of setting)

[will &satya 04/14/06]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#plot_data> "create a graphical representation of some data"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#plot_mass_spectrum_histogram> "create a histogram representation of a mass spectrum  (ion-peak abundance vs m/z)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#plot_raw_chromatogram> "create an x,y-plot of raw chromatogram data (time vs. signal intensity)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#plot_raw_mass_spectrum> "create an x,y-plot of raw mass spectral data (ion current vs m/z)"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#polynucleotide_accession_number> "A parameter that specifies the unique identifier in a database that refers to a particular gene or other nucleotide sequence. 

 [Dr. York & Satya: 06/24/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#potential_units> "A parameter defining the physical units of potential, such as electrical potential, gravitational potential, etc.
Potentials generally have units 'energy per amount', for example volts are Joules per Coulomb"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#power_units> "A parameter defining the physical units of power"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#procaryotic_organism> "An organism whose cells do not have a nucleus or internal membranes.

[Dr. York & Satya: 06/28/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#process_associated_data_collection> "A data collection that is classified according to the process that uses/creates/generates it."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#process_associated_parameter> "A parameter that is classified according to the process that uses/creates/generates it.

[will & satya 02/17/06]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#process_time_parameter> "A parameter that describes the time within a process that an event occured.  E.G., a 'retention time' in HPLC or a 'scan acquisition time' in mass spectrometry."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#processed_gel_electrophoresis_data> "A data collection generated by a processing raw gel electrophoresis data.  This data will include, for example
1. Spot location
2. Spot Intensity
3. Spot Identity

[Dr. York & Satya: 06/28/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#protein> "A biomolecule composed of amino acids connected by amide bonds.  In ProPreO, a protein is distinguished from an oligopeptide mainly by its size (proteins are larger, and so are polypeptides rather than oligopeptides) .

[Dr. York & Satya: 06/10/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#protein_accession_number> "A parameter that specifies the unique identifier for a particular protein in a database.

[Dr. York & Satya: 06/13/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#proteolytic_enzyme> "A  protein that catalyzes the cleavage of peptide bonds in proteins to generate peptides.

[Dr. York & Satya: 06/28/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#pure_substance> "A molecular aggregate composed of many copies of same molecule.

[will & satya 03/02/06]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#quadrupole_analyzer> "A type of MS analyzer"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#quadrupole_time_of_flight_mass_spectrometer> "A type of tandem_mass_spectrometer.

[James & Satya: 03/27/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#quantification> "The computational processing in which a quantity (e.g. amount) is associated with various data elements."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#quantification_paramter> "This describes the amount of particluar molecular species which is calculated from the raw data.

[Will & Satya 10/17/06]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#quaternary_HPLC_pump> "A type of HPLC pump.

[James & Satya: 01/31/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#raw2mzXML_transformation> "This task converts a raw mass spec data file into the mzXML format."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#raw_data_recording> "The task of recording raw data using an analytical instrument.

[Dr. York & Satya: 11/21/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#raw_gel_image_electrophoresis_data> "A data collection generated by a gel electrophoresis experiment - this corresponds to an image of the gel, stored in a file format.

[James & Satya: 03/29/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#representation_format_transformation> "The transformation of the representational format of data. For example, FASTA format to GCG format.

[Dr. York & Satya: 11/21/05]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#reversed-phase_HPLC_column> "A type of HPLC column"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#salt> "A chemical compound composed of at least one cation (positive ion) and at least one anion (negative ion)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#search_and_replacement> "A computational task involving the identification of specific data elements and their replacement by another data element."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#size_exclusion_HPLC_column> "A type of HPLC column"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#size_exclusion_chromatography> "The process of separating components by size-exclusion chromatography."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#small_molecule> "A molecule that is very generally classified by its small size.  This class is intended to allow the classification of molecules that are encountered in proteomics analysis (such as a solvent molecule or a MALDI matrix component), but are not classified as a major type of biomolecule."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#small_organic_molecule> "A small molecule that contains the element carbon."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#solid_mixture> "A mixture that is in the solid state, for example, dry baking powder, composed of solid NaHCO3 and tartaric acid.

[Satya & Will 03/02/06]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#solution> "A mixture in the form of a homogeneous liquid contaning a solvent and at least one solute.

 A 'solution' is_described_by one or more mixture_component_descriptor(s), each of which has two parts:  the component_amount and a substance_identifier that specifies the identity of the component.  This is a flexible way of describing solutions.  For example, a solution can be described as a mixture of two other solutions (e.g., buffer A and buffer B), in which case the mixture_component_descriptor(s) each specify the identity and amount of each of these buffers.  Alternatively, a solution can be described according to the concentrations of its solutes (dissolved molecules), each of which is specified by a mixture_component_descriptor.  In this case, complete description of the solution requires that the solvent be specified using the property has_solvent, which points to an instance of the class 'solvent'.
[Satya & Will 03/02/06]"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#solvent> "The solvent of a solution, consisting of many copies of the solvent molecule."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#solvent_molecule> "A molecule that exists as a liquid in the laboratory, and that can dissolve other molecules.  E.G. water, methanol."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#source_cell> "A parameter that specifies the cell type from which the biological sample is taken."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#source_organ> "A parameter that specifies the organ from which the biological sample is taken."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#source_organism> "A parameter that specifies the organism from which the biological sample is taken."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://lsdis.cs.uga.edu/projects/glycomics/propreo#statistical_analysis_parameter_collection> "For statistical analysis on any data, a set of parameters as input to the task.

